=== Introduction
--- Hold the Traditions? [title]
overline: Answering error
heading: Hold the Traditions?
sub: 2 Thessalonians 2 • The traditions of men • The Bereans • Another gospel
refs: 2 Thessalonians 2:15; Mark 7:13; Acts 17:11; Galatians 1:8
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== A proof text
--- The Complete Word of God
kicker: 2 Thessalonians 2
p: 2 Thessalonians 2 doesn't "refute Sola scriptura," (a term I hate.. It's just the Bible is the complete word of God).
p: Up front, any argument made that ignores the clear teachings of scripture, OT and NT, that scripture is inspired, preserved and complete "whole word of God," and directly from Jesus against holding to extra-scriptural traditions over scripture itself, is already proven wrong.
big: Proverbs 30:6 | mark: Add thou not unto his words
p: Many such cases.

--- Cherry Picking
kicker: 2 Thessalonians 2
p: People looking to defend heresy won't ever address the multiple instances of clear scripture that contradicts them, or explain with equally clear scripture how the first scripture is wrong.
p: What they do is cherry pick a single verse, out of context that if presented to unsaved people, ignorant of the Bible can maybe confuse them enough to see it their way.
p: 2 Thessalonians 2:15 is a perfect example of this. Ignoring the context of the epistle, and specifically the chapter it's pulled from, they will argue this:
big: 2 Thessalonians 2:15 | mark: hold the traditions which ye have been taught
p: ..trumps all scripture, and allows contrary teachings to scripture to supersede scripture.

--- A Foolish Argument
kicker: 2 Thessalonians 2
p: One, it's a foolish argument even taken as is. Paul would never tell Thessalonians to "stand fast" to a tradition that was preached to them in person, if it contradicts the word and epistles he just told them to hold to. That is absurd. "Wink wink, you know that secret stuff we told you but didn't write down? Yeah that says it's ok to worship idols and baptized babies and have a universal church controlled by men? Vain repetitive prayers? Works to be saved? Yeah hold on to that." It's not even a rational argument using the logic of men. Especially given the scriptures and epistles directly contradict the vain traditions of men being defended. This "proof text" alone contradicts the point being argued.
p: But taken in its context, it isn't even saying what is being alleged by the heretics.

=== In its context
--- The Day of Christ
kicker: 2 Thessalonians 2
scripture: 2 Thessalonians 2:1-3 | mark: That ye be not soon shaken in mind; Let no man deceive you by any means
p: Paul is writing to the independent NT church in Thessalonica with a specific message regarding a specific topic; End times prophecy.
p: We don't have to guess at what mystery doctrines were being given by these "traditions" given the church by word and epistle. Paul tells us in the second verse.
center: [[2 Thessalonians 2:1-17|Read 2 Thessalonians 2]]

--- Let No Man Deceive You
kicker: 2 Thessalonians 2
p: Judaizers and heretics, even in these first days of NT Christianity, were spreading lies and false doctrine that contradicted the scriptures. Paul is writing to reassure them and warn against it:
p: *Let no man deceive you by any means: for that day shall not come, except.*.. And he lists the order of events regarding the resurrection and coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.

--- When I Was Yet with You
kicker: 2 Thessalonians 2
big: 2 Thessalonians 2:5 | mark: when I was yet with you, I told you these things
p: Paul says "*Remember ye not, that, when I was yet with you, I told you these things?"* Reminding them of the in-person teaching he gave regarding this specific topic. Teachings that came from the Holy Ghost, through the gospel accounts of Christ's ministry and OT scriptures.
p: There were men trying to deceive them regarding the resurrection and return. He wrote to remind them of what was taught to them, giving us 2000yrs later the same instruction on the same doctrine.

--- Stand Fast
kicker: 2 Thessalonians 2
big: 2 Thessalonians 2:15 | mark: stand fast
p: *Therefore, brethren, stand fast, and hold the traditions which ye have been taught, whether by word, or our epistle.* Amen! Yes. Stand fast whether you learned this Biblical doctrine on the rapture and day of the Lord through preaching by an Apostle or evangelist gifted by the Holy Ghost, taken from scripture and the words of Christ, or by epistles. Amen!

--- Strong Delusion
kicker: 2 Thessalonians 2
p: All heretical doctrines and apologetics follow this pattern of stripping scripture of meaning, adding irrational argument to it, and ignoring the scriptures that contradicts their heresy. Just as I said.
p: What they will never do is post an entire chapter or book that surrounds their "proof text," and they won't ever attempt to square the differences with other scripture, just offer non sequitur citation and act as though it's an argument.
p: They may make an appeal to some 5th century "church fathers," but they won't ever use the whole word of God to defend their position. In fact, being unsaved and unable to understand scripture when shown, they act like robots in Westworld being shown a photo of modernity, "I don't see anything."

--- That They Should Believe a Lie
kicker: 2 Thessalonians 2
p: As Paul writes in **2 Thessalonians 2**, regarding Satan fooling unsaved people with false Gospels and doctrines:
scripture: 2 Thessalonians 2:10-12 | mark: because they received not the love of the truth; strong delusion, that they should believe a lie

=== Answering them
--- Not an Argument
kicker: Application • Answering error
p: Now it's important to note a few lessons for us, when we interact with unsaved people offering up false doctrines and using out of context scripture as "proof text."
p: This is a lesson it took me a while to learn, because we are trained in this era of social media to engage in an argument, to prove our side and own the other side. To enter into striving and debates about the law, answering foolish questions and other things that the scripture explicitly tells us not to do. It often leads to wrath, and wrath to sin. It's why the Bible tells us not to do it.

--- Correct Them with Love
kicker: Application • Answering error
p: And getting into a back and forth volley of proof text scriptures with someone who's unsaved is unprofitable and vain. Rather we should correct them with love from the scripture they're misusing, showing how it doesn't mean what they say it means using the word of God.
p: Keeping in mind they may be under a strong delusion, spiritual blindness which is a supernatural thing God does to some. It's why they can't see what you show them that contradicts their predetermined ideas.

--- A Zeal of God
kicker: Application • Answering error
p: Rather, like Paul says of the Jews, lamenting:
scripture: Romans 10:2-4 | mark: they have a zeal of God, but not according to knowledge
p: Many of these people are well meaning and have a zeal for God, even if it's in ignorance. We should pray that God opens their eyes and brings them understanding from his word, knowing that *faith cometh by hearing, and hearing by the word of God.* [[Romans 10:17]]
p: (Note, faith doesn't come from vain traditions of men but by His word, scripture. The Bible)

--- Shake the Dust Off
kicker: Application • Answering error
p: This is why I have the rules I have in my chat. It's not an invitation to an argument when somebody contradicts biblical fundamentalism to pull out an extra scriptural doctrine. We are to correct and rebuke them, and if they accept it we can go on. But if they cannot see it there is no point in continuing the discussion. Rather we should shake the dust off and move on.
scripture: 2 Timothy 3:16-17 | mark: All scripture is given by inspiration of God

=== The traditions of men
--- The Tradition of the Elders
kicker: Mark 7
p: Biblical fundamentalism and the rejection of traditions of men, as taught by Jesus Christ.
scripture: Mark 7:5-7 | mark: Why walk not thy disciples according to the tradition of the elders; teaching for doctrines the commandments of men
center: [[Mark 7:1-23|Read Mark 7:1–23]]

--- Making the Word of God of None Effect
kicker: Mark 7
p: Key points of Jesus preaching in Mark 7:
scripture: Mark 7:8-9; Mark 7:13 | mark: ye hold the tradition of men; Making the word of God of none effect through your tradition
p: Making the word of God, which is scripture, *of none effect through your tradition*.

--- Corban
kicker: Mark 7
scripture: Mark 7:10-12 | mark: It is Corban
p: He uses an example of the Jews tradition, allowing a son to dishonor their parents by declaring their wealth "Corban," or a gift to the temple while keeping and using the wealth for themselves. But this applies to ANY extra-scriptural doctrines and traditions that contradicts the word of God. Making God's word to none effect by their traditions.
p: There is your Biblical "Sola scriptura" doctrine (cringe Latin term for biblical fundamentalism) straight from Jesus Christ Himself.
p: Any tradition of man that contradicts scripture is heresy. Period.

=== Out of the scriptures
--- Reasoned with Them out of the Scriptures
kicker: Acts 17
p: The Book of Acts shows that the Apostles and those given the gift of the Holy Ghost, evangelists, who went out to preach the word of God and the Gospel, the Good news of Christ, taught the doctrine of Christ from scripture.
p: **Acts 17** details this well:
scripture: Acts 17:2-3 | mark: reasoned with them out of the scriptures
center: [[Acts 17:1-17|Read Acts 17:1–17]]

--- More Noble
kicker: Acts 17
big: Acts 17:11 | mark: searched the scriptures daily, whether those things were so
p: People who don't read the Bible and can't understand it if they do, will often make sweeping claims that their heretical ideas and false doctrines must be true based on some twisted logic of man. Claims that simply knowing the Bible easily refute.

--- No Secret Traditions
kicker: Acts 17
p: They claim because the Gospel was preached orally that there were secret traditions given that were in conflict with clear teaching from scripture, when in fact what was preached was from scripture. Jesus is the fulfilment of the OT. The Law. The promise to Abraham. And scripture is how we know this is true. Just as Paul and the apostles used scripture to convert the Thessalonians here in Acts 17, and just as he wrote to them in epistles to stand fast to the teachings from scripture that he gave them in person in 2 Thessalonians 2.
p: He gave them no instruction or tradition that contradicted scripture or else how would they search *the scriptures daily, whether those things were so?*
p: The proof text Catholics use to denigrate the word of God and justify their damnable heresies behind "tradition," is undone by simply reading the word.
big: Proverbs 30:6

=== Another gospel
--- Necessary for Salvation?
kicker: Galatians 1
quote: The Church affirms that for believers the sacraments of the New Covenant are necessary for salvation. | The Catholic catechism
p: This is blasphemy and damnable heresy.
p: It is blasphemy and damnable heresy because it directly contradicts the Bible. It is another gospel.

--- Let Him Be Accursed
kicker: Galatians 1
scripture: Galatians 1:8-9 | mark: let him be accursed
p: Notice, Paul writing to the Galatians in the Spirit, God inspired scripture, says this TWICE. For emphasis.
p: And what was it he preached to the Galatians?

--- Not after Man
kicker: Galatians 1
scripture: Galatians 1:11-12 | mark: the gospel which was preached of me is not after man; but by the revelation of Jesus Christ
center: [[Galatians 1:10-24|Read Galatians 1:10–24]]
p: Don't miss this, Paul makes it emphatically clear he didn't learn any secret traditions of man from any Apostles. He wasn't told what to say by anyone else. He, knowing the scriptures and having by the grace of God the opportunity for salvation in Jesus, was given all to preach to the heathen.

--- Not by the Works of the Law
kicker: Galatians 2
p: He explains how, after 14 years the issue of Judaizers and the circumcision brought him to go to Jerusalem and talk to the local church there, run by James BTW, and they agreed to send letters out denouncing the judaizers adding works to salvation, and affirming the Gospel:
big: Galatians 2:16 | mark: a man is not justified by the works of the law, but by the faith of Jesus Christ
p: This is the Gospel. And ANY MAN bringing any other Gospel, especially of works and rites for salvation, IS ACCURSED.

--- The Whole Word of God
kicker: Application • The Bible alone
p: So, according to scripture from which ALL doctrine is to be taken, so that a man of God can be perfect, complete, and throughly furnished unto all good works, the whole word of God, the Catholic Church that has added to the word, has given another Gospel, is accursed.
p: We don't need so-called saints, endorsed by an accursed institution like the pagan church of Rome, to explain doctrine to us. We don't need extra biblical instruction on vain traditions of man that contradicts clear scripture from the word of God. We don't need anything but the word of God and the Spirit that indwells all believers when they are born again in faith alone, filled with grace from the living God.

--- He Shall Teach You All Things
kicker: Application • The Bible alone
p: We have the Holy Spirit, who IS God.
big: John 14:26 | mark: he shall teach you all things

